+  early_stop_windows: [1h]  # 2026-08-09 RESTORED to [1h] (was reverted to [all] by the baseline restore, which re-armed the fast-window winner-cutter; it fired once this session on xrp 15m entry 0.91 -> cut 0.665 -$20.60, the session's biggest single loss = the exact documented failure mode). [1h] = 5m/15m ride to resolution, only doge-1h keeps the stop. STAGED not restarted. 2026-08-08 WINDOW-CONDITIONAL EARLY STOPS (operator GO; held-projection this session). The early hold-lane cuts — favorite_hard_stop (above) AND the independent hold_catastrophic_stop backstop — fire ONLY on these windows; other windows ride to resolution. Default 1h. WHY: the stop-hold sweep (this session) showed 5m/15m winners routinely dip to -20..-46% MAE mid-window and STILL settle GREEN (sol 15m held +114.73 vs stopped +105.65; xrp 15m +131.86 vs +124.02; hype 15m +83.84 vs +78.72) — so a mark stop on fast windows is structurally guaranteed to cut winners (this is the SAME finding as the autowake 15m bust note on hard_stop_price above). doge 1h is the LONE lane where HOLDING LOSES (-26.62 vs +8.49 stopped, delta -35.11) => 1h KEEPS the stop. The final-seconds presettle de-risk is a SEPARATE block and stays active on every window. Tokens: "all" => keep stop on every window (pre-change behavior); [] => keep it nowhere. RESTART-CLASS (execution code, not hot-reloadable).
