codex
The first diff confirms the current config is not a clean 08-09 continuation: several 08-10/08-11 controls are mixed in, and `risk.favorite_lane_enabled:false` now hot-kills favorite signals while `favorite_lane.enabled:true` still sits below it. I’m narrowing this to actual code paths and session economics rather than trusting inline comments.
exec
/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n "favorite_lane_enabled|rsi_fade|regime_fade|size_taper|fav_net_sit_out|hold_mfe_conditional|tp_giveback|early_stop_windows|hold_never_green|take_profit_giveback|favorite_hard_stop|hold_catastrophic" config/settings.yaml src/strategies/bitcoin.py src/strategies/sol_macro.py src/execution/live_testing.py' in /Users/mainfolder/Documents/psb-main 1
 succeeded in 0ms:
config/settings.yaml:85:  max_position_size: 40   # 2026-08-10 KEEP 40 as the CEILING (operator caught: 25 would clamp the proven winning lanes). $40 is the HARD CAP; base bets stay Kelly-small; the SELECT WINNING lanes reach $35-40 via adaptive_sizer.proven_lane_max_usd (40) + lane_max_usd (bitcoin15mYES 35, bnb15mNO/xrp15mNO 40, ...). +869 geometry = achieved via KILLING the favorite lane (risk.favorite_lane_enabled:false), NOT by capping the winners. Do NOT drop to 25 — it strangles the winning-lane sizing.
config/settings.yaml:449:    hold_catastrophic_stop_pct: 0.55   # EXIT-ASYMMETRY 08-07: cap losers at -55% (now FIRES independently under hold_all, was inert). Below observed winner worst-MAE -51% so it cuts genuine failures, not recoverable dips. Enables safe size-up.
config/settings.yaml:451:    # Ghost-settled the 130 hold_catastrophic_stop trades held-to-resolution: 88% (105/120) still resolve to $0 —
config/settings.yaml:455:    # green (peak MFE < arm) is cut SHALLOW at hold_never_green_stop_pct instead of riding to the -55% catastrophic;
config/settings.yaml:458:    hold_mfe_conditional_stop_enabled: true   # 2026-08-10 STAGED (Codex round-2 GO) — never-green (peak MFE<8%) cut shallow -34%, ever-green rides. Codex round-1 NO-GO (bypasses [1h] window axis on fast windows) was REFUTED by the ghost split: held (updown_expired) counterfactual shows never-green 5m/15m that dip past -34% recover 0/14 (100% resolve to a loss), while ever-green 5m/15m ride at 90% WR. Cutting the 14 dead losers: -$188 -> -$62 (+$126, zero winners forfeited). This is the "$16 never-green loss -> $5 cut" fix. STAGED not restarted (frozen at live_testing.__init__ — takes effect on next restart). _is_fav>=0.82 exemption is a cleanup note (favorite generators return [] when favorite_lane_enabled:false).
config/settings.yaml:459:    hold_never_green_mfe_arm: 0.08     # peak MFE >= +8% => "ever green" (rides); below => never-green (cut shallow)
config/settings.yaml:460:    hold_never_green_stop_pct: 0.34    # shallow cut depth for never-green non-favorite losers (~restores June discipline)
config/settings.yaml:463:    tp_giveback_enabled: false  # 2026-08-11 RIPPED (operator: "rip out the bullshit bandaids I don't need"). Feed-blind: proven this session it MISSES the give-backs it was built for (every big BNB give-back had mae==exit = no intervening tick observed, so a reactive trail can't bank a retrace it never sees). Confirmed-peak/green-floor sub-patches are now dead code (fire-condition first clause is self._tp_giveback_enabled). The ever-green MFE stop is the real exit fix and stays ON.  # 2026-08-10 RE-ENABLED (operator: "+108 to nothing is not okay"). The 08-09 off-decision was made on 4 fires, 2 of which were the RARE settlement-gap failure. Re-measured on the FULL log: of 200 give-backs (peak>=30% then lost), 96% are WALK-DOWNS the trail banks; only 4% are gaps. Both live BNB give-backs (1h YES peak +108% and +72%) are walk-downs -> trail converts -$15.21 to +$15.68 (+$31 swing). Only the 2 bitcoin-15m fade give-backs gap (trail misses those; separate fix). STAGED (frozen at init) -> rides the MFE-cond restart. WATCH first live fires bank real green.  # 2026-08-09 ENABLED (operator GO). ROOT of the deep-loss bleed: 74% of Aug catastrophic-stops were EVER-GREEN round-trips (median peaked +50% -> died -65%); 77 Aug losses peaked >=+30% then round-tripped (-$611). This banks a reversing winner on a >=retrace(0.20) from peak(>=arm 0.30) => exits >=+10% green instead of riding to -55%/-68% catastrophic. Fires UNDER hold (reason take_profit_giveback NOT in the hold-enforce suppression tuple). Only fires on a REAL retrace so a still-climbing runner is never cut (the 07-13/07-16 fixed-trail failure mode is avoided). Projected +~$977 swing on the 77 round-trip losses. WATCH first fires = banking real green not phantom-mark noise.
config/settings.yaml:485:    proven_lane_max_usd: 40   # 2026-08-10 (operator): was 0 (off). Proven lanes (WR>=proven_wr_min 0.55 AND ROI>=proven_roi_min 0.05) cap at $40 = the "max bet 35-40 on select WINNING lanes". Unproven/losing lanes stay small (unproven_lane_mult 0.6) + regime_fade sits out <48% WR.
config/settings.yaml:584:regime_fade:
config/settings.yaml:585:  enabled: true    # 2026-08-10 ENABLED (operator GO). Per-lane PER-SIDE auto-sitout when a lane's rolling WR collapses below fade_below_wr (0.48) in the mid-confidence band [0.45,0.65) — the eth NATIVE-LONG bleed (37% WR, -$136) is exactly this: momentum longs run over in a chop/down tape while the ≥0.65 favorites are protected. Adaptive/self-flipping (resumes when WR recovers >0.53), fail-open. Was left OFF; fade_regime_windows also empty (fade never fired) → bot ran native momentum, the known loser. RESTART-CLASS (regime_fade not in _HOT_RELOAD_TOP_LEVEL_KEYS).
config/settings.yaml:2369:  size_taper_enabled: true   # 2026-08-09 #2 SIZE-TAPER (operator GO): scale stake by payoff (1-fav_price)/(1-floor); 0.85 fav=full, 0.93 fav=~0.47x. Scope: 0.88-0.91 band 71%WR but -$111 (thin payoff); recovers ~+$50, zero trades cut. RESTART-CLASS (code).
config/settings.yaml:2370:  size_taper_min_frac: 0.4   # floor on the taper (never below 40% of size_usd)
config/settings.yaml:2371:  size_taper_start: 0.88     # full size up to 0.88 (the +$72 sweet spot); taper only 0.88->0.93 (the bleed bands)
config/settings.yaml:2377:  hard_stop_price: 0.70    # 2026-08-08 06:1x DISABLED (was 0.70) — AUTOWAKE REVERT, it cut WINNERS 3-for-3 in its first 4 minutes live. Session test_20260808_060714, the 9:00-9:15AM ET window: sol entry 0.86 cut 0.695 -$15.41 | btc entry 0.90 cut 0.415 -$39.75 (the paged bust) | xrp entry 0.86 cut 0.675 -$17.09 = -$72.25 realized. CLOB prices-history says ALL THREE Up tokens settled 0.995 (WON): sol 0.875->0.685 dip->0.995, btc 0.705->0.755->0.995, xrp whipsaw->0.995. doge (control, same window, never dipped below 0.90) was never cut and won. A 15m favorite bought at 0.85-0.93 routinely dips to 0.60-0.70 mid-window and still settles 1.0 — a 0.70 mark stop is structurally guaranteed to cut the lane's winners, which IS the lane's 94%-WR edge (hold to resolution). The btc one is worse still: it fired on mark 0.415 (best_bid 0.41/ask 0.42, ws age 6.9ms) at 13:09:44 when the real tape was ~0.62-0.755 — a mark that never existed, after 106s where the position was invisible to check_exits (mfe=0.0, mae==exit pnl => not one intervening tick was evaluated). 0 => off; loss control reverts to hold_catastrophic_stop_pct -55% + the presettle de-risk above (the config the proven favorite lane ran in). Do NOT re-enable without evidence from settled favorites that a mid-window dip below 0.70 actually predicts a LOSS.
config/settings.yaml:2378:  early_stop_windows: [1h]  # 2026-08-09 RESTORED to [1h] (was reverted to [all] by the baseline restore, which re-armed the fast-window winner-cutter; it fired once this session on xrp 15m entry 0.91 -> cut 0.665 -$20.60, the session's biggest single loss = the exact documented failure mode). [1h] = 5m/15m ride to resolution, only doge-1h keeps the stop. STAGED not restarted. 2026-08-08 WINDOW-CONDITIONAL EARLY STOPS (operator GO; held-projection this session). The early hold-lane cuts — favorite_hard_stop (above) AND the independent hold_catastrophic_stop backstop — fire ONLY on these windows; other windows ride to resolution. Default 1h. WHY: the stop-hold sweep (this session) showed 5m/15m winners routinely dip to -20..-46% MAE mid-window and STILL settle GREEN (sol 15m held +114.73 vs stopped +105.65; xrp 15m +131.86 vs +124.02; hype 15m +83.84 vs +78.72) — so a mark stop on fast windows is structurally guaranteed to cut winners (this is the SAME finding as the autowake 15m bust note on hard_stop_price above). doge 1h is the LONE lane where HOLDING LOSES (-26.62 vs +8.49 stopped, delta -35.11) => 1h KEEPS the stop. The final-seconds presettle de-risk is a SEPARATE block and stays active on every window. Tokens: "all" => keep stop on every window (pre-change behavior); [] => keep it nowhere. RESTART-CLASS (execution code, not hot-reloadable).
config/settings.yaml:2381:  fav_net_sit_out_avg: -1.0   # 2026-08-10 FAVORITE-SCOPED REALIZED-NET SIT-OUT (operator GO). Sit out a favorite (asset,window,side) while its rolling AVG realized net per favorite close <= this ($/trade). Reads favorite_net_tracker (FAVORITE-only closes, entry>=floor, keyed asset|window|side) — NOT lane_tape_adapter (which mixes favorite+band + is MFE/green not NET, so it read sol|15m|up as loosen while it bled -$99). Payoff-trap aware (favorites are high-WR/neg-NET). Validated on journal: -1.0 sits out doge15mDOWN(-6.3) xrp15mUP(-4.4) bnb1hUP(-3.5) sol1hDOWN(-2.2) etc; KEEPS xrp1h(+6.6) sol15mUP(+3.5). Self-flips: rolling window rolls losers off / recovery re-admits. null/absent => OFF (fail-open). RESTART-CLASS (favorite_lane not hot-reloadable).
config/settings.yaml:2503:  favorite_lane_enabled: false   # 2026-08-10 KILL THE FAVORITE LANE (operator: revert to +869 winning config, which had NO favorite lane). Favorites 0.85+ = win-11%/lose-90% payoff-trap, b=0.13, need 88% WR, −$448 all-time. Under `risk` = HOT-RELOADABLE (no restart). Set true to re-enable. Read by sol_macro + bitcoin _favorite_lane_signals.
config/settings.yaml:2504:  rsi_fade:                # 2026-08-10 RSI-GATED COINFLIP FADE (operator GO — the MEASURED >coinflip edge, project_rsi_fade_edge_found_2026_08_10). Under `risk` so it's HOT-RELOADABLE => REVERT TRIGGER = flip enabled:false (no restart) if fade-WR < breakeven. Read by sol_macro._resolve_alt_bias_for_tf (shared by ALL alts + eth): fades the direction-lane side when RSI < rsi_below AND trend NOT fully-aligned (align-gate = regime safety; fading a strong aligned trend gets run over). Favorites bypass the resolver = UNAFFECTED. Measured: RSI<40 native 30%WR => FADE 69.6% (4 sessions, never <56%). rsi_above 101 = overbought-fade OFF (ship strongest zone first). side_source retagged *_rsi_fade for attribution/monitoring.
